  "id": "COMPOUND:31583 - PROTEIN:5837",
  "verbalization": "Visnagin is implicated in a complex network of interactions leading to SN12K1 through the UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2A1 enzyme. This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including Quercetin Glucuronide and Cyclopentadecanone, both of which are involved in the metabolism of their respective substrates. The presence of a highly specific and long-chain substrate, [(1R,5R,6R,8R,9S,11S,12S,15S,16R,18S)-5-acetyloxy-6-benzamido-15-[(1S)-1-(dimethylamino)ethyl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethyl-19-oxapentacyclo[9.8.0.01,18.03,8.012,16]nonadec-3-en-9-yl] acetate, further supports the notion that UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2A1 is a critical mediator in the pathway from Visnagin to SN12K1. The cumulative evidence suggests that Visnagin may influence SN12K1 through the modulation of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2A1, which in turn affects the metabolic fate of various substrates. The integration of these pathways highlights the enzyme's role as a central node in the metabolic network, with potential implications for drug development targeting this enzyme.",
